++## Durable adapter-instance record
++
++Every spawned process has an `adapter_instances` row in `kernel-store-schema.sql`: `adapter_instance_id`, exact `(adapter_id, adapter_version, bundle_digest)` (FK to `adapter_registrations`), `daemon_instance_id`, `pid`, `process_start_identity`, `state` with persisted literals `starting`, `ready`, `exited`, `failed`, `exit_reason`, `last_heartbeat_ms`, `started_at_ms`, and `ended_at_ms`. A restart creates a new row and never mutates the prior instance; old in-flight protocol sessions are invalid.
++
+ ## Spawn contract
+ 
+ Input includes:
+ 
+ - expected immutable bundle digest;
+ - executable path from installed bundle;
+ - argv;
+ - minimal environment allowlist;
